<section class="section shell" id="itineraries">
  <div class="kicker">Make the most of your day</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Itineraries</h2>
  <p>Choose a route that fits your group and pace. All options start from the monument inside Iqbal Park.</p>

  <h3 class="block-title">By type of traveller</h3>
  <div class="info-grid">
    <div class="card"><h4 class="route-name">Families with children</h4><p>Confirm a usable route, barriers, toilets and a rest option before taking children. Keep children away from water and restricted areas; a flat, shaded or stroller-accessible circuit is not guaranteed.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4 class="route-name">Photography &amp; nature</h4><p>Confirm permitted visitor hours and photography or tripod rules before planning a shoot. Sunrise, sunset or historical illumination photos do not authorize access outside the current gate times.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4 class="route-name">Low-effort / accessible</h4><p>Maps indicated an accessible entrance on 29 October 2026, but the exact gate and route have not been independently confirmed. Ask about steps, surfaces, seating, assistance and distance for your needs before travelling.</p></div>
  </div>

  <h3 class="block-title" style="margin-top:2.5rem">General routes</h3>
  <div class="info-grid">
    <div class="card"><h4 class="route-name">Half-day</h4><p>Consider the monument and permitted park areas first, then one separately confirmed old-city destination such as Delhi Gate or Wazir Khan Mosque. Check routes and hours rather than relying on a measured half-day circuit.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4 class="route-name">Full-day</h4><p>A full-day idea can combine the monument with selected old-city sites, Badshahi Mosque or Lahore Fort. Each has separate entry rules, hours and transport; do not assume all fit in one day or that an evening return is allowed.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section dark" id="history">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="kicker" style="color:#e5b55f">Background &amp; stories</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">History &amp; Significance</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p><strong>{d.fullName}</strong> stands on the ground where, on 23 March 1940, the All-India Muslim League passed the Lahore Resolution — the formal demand for a separate homeland for the Muslims of the subcontinent. The site was then part of Minto Park, later renamed Iqbal Park after the poet-philosopher Allama Iqbal.</p>
        <p>The foundation stone was laid on the same date in 1960, and the monument was completed in 1968. It was designed by architect Nasreddin Murat-Khan, who migrated to Pakistan and shaped a structure that blends Islamic, Mughal and modernist motifs.</p>
        <p>The tower rises above a series of petal-shaped platforms &ldquo;unfolding&rdquo; from the ground — widely read as a symbol of a nation coming into being. Inscriptions at the base include the text of the Pakistan Resolution and verses, and the different stone and marble tiers are said to reflect the stages of the struggle.</p>
        <p>Today the monument is a civic gathering point, a photography landmark and a reminder of the political moment that reshaped the region.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="photo-frame"><img src="/images/minar.jpg" width="1280" height="960" alt="Minar-e-Pakistan, historical 2011 photograph" loading="lazy"/><figcaption class="credits">Zpotrick · 16 February 2011 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minar_e_Pakistan_(Lahore).jpg">source</a> · <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/">CC BY-SA 3.0</a> · unmodified file; display may crop. Does not establish current tower access.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="responsibility" style="background:#e7ddc8">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="kicker">Visit responsibly</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Respect &amp; Visitor Responsibility</h2>
    <div class="info-grid">
      <div class="card"><h3 class="block-title">Protect the monument</h3><p>Do not climb restricted areas or mark the stonework. Keep to paths and railings so the structure and gardens stay intact for everyone.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3 class="block-title">Dress &amp; conduct</h3><p>Modest attire is appropriate at this civic and cultural site. Keep noise low near gatherings and ask before photographing people.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3 class="block-title">Reduce your footprint</h3><p>Carry a reusable bottle, take litter home or use bins, and avoid single-use plastics where you can. The park is a shared green space.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3 class="block-title">Health &amp; safety</h3><p>In winter smog season, sensitive groups should check air quality and carry a mask. Secure valuables in crowded areas, and hydrate in the summer heat.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

